show grogu his potential in  wielding the force luke even brings back  some of yoda's famous phrases like size  matters not and a tweaked version of do  or do not there is no try in another  scene luke wears grogu in a backpack and  runs leaps and flips through the bamboo  forest before climbing up a stalk to  show grogu how beautiful and vast this  planet and the whole galaxy can be this  quick paced scene is a direct nod to  luke doing the same thing with yoda on  his back  in the book of boba fett episode 7 the  season finale a new type of battle droid  is introduced the scorpenectroid the  pike syndicate unleashes two of these  huge and deadly droids on boba fett's  crew while they try to fight off the  pikes and protect mose espa luckily boba  has a rancor and a little green force  sensitive who can help him take down  these droids and win the war for boba  fett and crew in the star wars legends  continuity scorpenectroids were used by  the separatists during the clone wars  along with the familiar droidikas both  types of droids had rapid-fire laser  cannons and deployed nearly impenetrable  deflector shields the scorpenec droid  was first mentioned in the book the new  essential guide to droids and its  concept art appears to be an early form  of what would become the droidica in  star wars attack of the clones  boba fett and cadbane have a long  history dating back to the prequel era  and the latter learned the bounty  hunting ways from the former's father  jango fett the two bounty hunters have  had a tolerate hate relationship for  decades and they reunite in the book of  boba fett episode 7. boba is working for  himself and his people and bane is being  paid by the pikes to enforce the flow of  spice in the area this leads to a battle  between the two parties and an epic duel  between boba and bane the duel ends in  boba's favor with him stabbing bane with  his tuscan gaffy stick interestingly the  clash echoes the one from an unfinished  episode of the clone wars in the unaired  arc the duel between the two bounty  hunters shows them squaring off on  tatooine and shooting each other the  unfinished scene shows how boba got the  circular dent in his helmet which is  still there even after being repainted  though it wasn't clear in the unfinished  episode bane appears in the bad batch  with a metal plate on his head hinting  that boba shot him in the head during  the duel in the book of boba fett season  finale the metal plate is shown again  when bane's hat is knocked off all but  confirming the unfinished episode is  part of the canon  before their final duel in chapter seven  boba fett and cad bane trade barbs in a  nod to their fraught history over the  decades at one point bane says  if that's not the quack to call in the  stiffling slimy  that's basically the star wars version  of the pot calling the kettle black and  it's not the first time we've heard this  phrase in a star wars television series  in the mandalorian season 2 finale din  and boba meet with bo katan kris and  koska reeves to enlist their help in  rescuing grogu from the imperial  clutches of moff gideon with all four of  them being mandalorians in some way they  all have different views on the way  mandalorians should act as such the two  women don't like boba and he doesn't  like them while trading barbs before  their weapons come out koska says i  didn't know sidekicks were allowed to  talk boba responds by saying well if  that isn't the quack to calling the  stiffling slimy boba's remark is meant  to poke at koska's place as bogotan's  sidekick but it seems the phrase is  pretty popular among bounty hunters  with the conclusion of season 1 of the  book of boba fett the clone and  ex-bounty hunter is now the godfather of  tatooine fittingly in the season finale  there are two key callbacks to the  godfather films the first comes when  boba sends the former mayor's twilike  major domo out to share his terms of  surrender with the pikes the major domo  reads boba's words on his tablet telling  the pikes he offers them nothing this  speech echoes the one by michael  corleone in the godfather part 2. you  can have my answer now if you like  my offer is this  nothing  and in the end of the episode after boba  and his crew win the battle and restore  peace he and fennick walk the streets of  mo's espa one citizen comes up to boba  and offers him a melee run fruit which  boba gives to chrysanton this moment is  a subtle nod to don corleone receiving  gifts of fruit from those he ruled over  in the godfather 2 but in filming style  it's arguably more reminiscent of the  simpsons parody of the godfather 2. don  hopper i have baked a special donut just  for you  since the premiere of return of the jedi  in 1983 fans have been wondering if and  how boba fed escaped the sarlacc pit and  the retconned star wars legends  continuity boba escapes the pit using  his jet pack as seen in the 1983 comic  star wars number 81 titled jawas of doom  and in the 1996 story a barf like that  boba also escapes the sarlacc via his  jetpack this time by telepathically  communicating with another victim inside  the beast and tricking the creature into  launching his weapon boba's canonical  escape from the sarlacc in episode 1 of  the book of boba fett is similar to the  legends one but in the book of boba fett  the iconic bounty hunter unleashes a  flamethrower on his wrist gauntlet to  burn the creature from the inside and  claw his way up through the deep sandy  pit  blink and you'll miss the wreckage of  jabba the hutt's iconic sailing barge  the katana in the scene of boba fett  emerging from the sarlacc pit in episode  1. in the original trilogies finale film  the chaotic fighting and the epic death  of jabba at the hands of leia also  resulted in the destruction of the  katana destroyed beyond repair and no  longer with a captain it was left to rot  on the sands above the pit of carcoon in  the book of boba fett the remains of the  destroyed barge can be seen behind boba  at the edge of the pit as he claws his  way to the surface and collapses on the  sand where sure the katana has been  picked clean of any valuables over the  years by some jawas just as they do to  an unconscious boba in the first episode  the mysterious spider droid carrying a  fishbowl of orange red liquid is  actually a member of the ancient bomar  order a religious sect whose members  transplanted their brains into these  bowls and used these spider droids to  move about in order to focus all  sensation and attention on their minds a  bomar order spider droid first appeared  in return of the jedi in 1983 in a short  scene that shows one of them walking by  an open door in jabba's palace according  to star wars lore these monks were the  original owners of the palace and  mozespa until jabba took over in the  book of boba fett it appears there are  still some members of the bomar order  left on tatooine as the opening scene of  episode 3 shows a spider droid scuttling  past the exterior of the palace  are these the droids you're looking for  in the book of boba fett's first episode  two droids in particular stood out hd8  and r3x aka rex 8d8 is a humanoid-esque  smelter droid that was last seen as a  torturer in return of the jedi in the  book of boba fett 88 is now a butler of  sorts helping introduce the colors  coming to greet and pay tribute to  tatooine's new crime lord the droid's  mention of tortured screams of the  gomorian guards he drags in is a subtle  nod to his previous sadistic role for  jabba those two gomorian guards are also  very likely the same ones who served  jabba in return of the jedi these two  gomorians were once body guides to jabba  the hat and later bib fortuna  they did not surrender even after their  patron was killed  the other recognizable droid r3x is  lifted from disney's theme parks in  particular galaxy's edge at disney world  and disneyland r3x had a long history as  the fun pilot of star tours but most  recently took another gig as a dj at  ogus cantina in blackspire outpost in  the book of boba fed r3x is seen playing  a dealer at the most espa casino  a tatooine cantina wouldn't be the same  without the planet's most famous tunes  luckily the book of boba fett brings  back two of the galaxy's most famous  musicians for a hefty dose of nostalgia  inside the moe's espa venue patrons are  imbibing and betting while a funky remix  of the classic cantina band song is  played by none other than max rebo and  figrin dan max rebo is a blue skinned  elephant-like creature who is  understandably presumed dead after last  being seen on jabba's sailing barge but  it looks like he's alive and well  alongside figure and dan the bith  musician a former member of the popular  band figure and dan and the modal nodes  played cantina band in the iconic scene  and mows eisley in a new hope though  he's without his other band members and  in a new town figrin dan seems to be  doing just fine playing tunes at the  moe's espa cantina with max rebo  boba fett may be down and out during his  imprisonment by the tuscan raiders but  he still knows how to kill a foe like  the best of them when he and a fellow  prisoner a rhodian dig for black melons  in the tattooing desert in episode 1 the  rodian awakens a multi-armed scaly beast  that attacks them and the young tuscan  raider they're with the goro-like  creature quickly kills the rodian and  goes after boba and the tuscan raider  next but boba uses his shackles and  chain to his advantage in a move  straight out of return of the jedi boba  swings the chain around the beast's neck  and pulls tight strangling it until it  falls he stands triumphantly atop the  creature holding his chains and  glowering at the tuscan raider it's a  moment where boba earns some respect  from his captors but also one eerily  similar to the way princess leia killed  jabba the hutt by strangling him with  her chains  showrunner and director robert rodriguez  has a key cameo in the series premiere  stranger in a strange land rodriguez  portrays dog strassie the leader of the  trandocian family who works under jabba  the hutt on tatooine in the first  episode dokstrassi greets boba and gives  him a tribute in the form of wookie pelt  during the exchange boba remarks on the  awkwardness of the situation since he  had worked for the trendocion at one  point in his bounty hunting career and  now dokstrassi serves him as joke stress  he leaves the throne room of now boba's  palace he tells him may you never leave  mo's espa even when a trend ocean pays  you a compliment it sounds like a threat  one of the most jaw-dropping moments in  the book of boba fett is the surprise  live-action introduction of wookie  gladiator black cursantin in episode 2  the tribes of tatooine star wars comics  fans know the towering all-black wookie  gladiator and bounty hunter black  chrysanthemum from when he was  introduced in 2015 in marvel's darth  vader series black chrysanthen also  known as santi bk and black k is also a  fan favorite character in the dr aphra  comics in the lore shown in the comics  black cursantin was taken from his  homeworld of kashyyyk and trained to be  a gladiator in fighting pits black  chrysanthen eventually becomes a bounty  hunter and works for jabba and at one  point works alongside boba fett it's  likely moses espa's new boss knows  exactly what the ruthless wookie is  capable of when they reunite in episode  2.  it might be a little late for luke  skywalker to snag some power converters  but it wasn't too late for star wars to  reveal tashi's station and show what the  jedi's childhood best friends are up to  take these two over to the garage will  you i want them cleaned up for dinner  but i was going into toshi station to  pick up some power converters you can  waste time with your friends when your  chores are done while boba fett brings  an epic beat down to the local menacing  swoop bike gang in episode 2 two humans  are cowering and trying to avoid the  mayhem these two humans a man and a  woman are never named in the episode but  they are most certainly luke's friends  cami and fixer and this small cantina is  toshi station the brief shots of the  building's exterior and interior  architecture show details that match the  deleted scene of toshi station from the  first star wars movie in 1977. for those  original details from the original film  kami and fixer were around luke's age  and hung out often at tashi station kami  is also referenced in the last jedi  novel when luke dreams about what his  life would have been like if he never  left tatooine and married cammy instead  though their appearances are brief the  cammy and fixer cameos are a fun subtle  nod to original star wars details that  ended up on the cutting room floor  being such a star wars fan it's no  surprise that executive producer robert  rodriguez has made more than one cameo  in the show in episode two that comes in  the form of moze espa's ethorian mayor  who may or may not have hired an  assassin to take out or test boba fett  in episode one the mayor's major domo  appears in boba's new court as a  representative of the mayor's office  both boba and fenik shand feel insulted  by the mayor not coming himself but in  episode two the two groups finally meet  the mayor is mock chaiez an ethorian who  communicates via a translator headpiece  aka the voice of rodriguez  is that so  i've heard otherwise  the mayor rebuffs boba's and fenix  allegations that he sent an assassin  after him and even thanks boba for  bringing in the assassin for punishment  he's quickly executed besides handing  boba and fennick a sack of coins mayor  mock chaiez offers his tribute of advice  about running a family and tells him to  see madame garceth whip for the latest  news about his position on mo's espa  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  star wars are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

